From c3485835c263e32a108dbd84164d4eaef7c65266 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Attard <sam@electronjs.org>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 20:58:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix: keep hidden windows rendering when they navigate
 (#54090)

* fix: keep hidden windows rendering when they navigate

A window created with `show: false` could stop producing frames as a
page committed, so `ready-to-show` never fired and the app stayed
invisible until something else showed the window. With a
`titleBarOverlay` this regressed in 44.4.0 (#54025); calling
`setZoomFactor()` on a hidden window before its first paint hit the same
thing since 40 (#51972).

Electron keeps such a window's widget visible so it can paint while the
native view is hidden. RenderWidgetHostViewAura::DidNavigate only looked
at the view, decided the widget was dormant and invalidated its
LocalSurfaceId, so any VisualProperties update sent before the first
frame was acked (the overlay rect posted from DidFinishNavigation since
#53639, or a zoom change) reached the renderer without a surface id and
it deferred all main frames until the window was shown.

Key the DidNavigate decision off the host's visibility as well, which is
what RenderWidgetHostViewMac already does, so a widget that is still
painting keeps a valid surface id across navigations.

* test: don't wait for an initial geometrychange in the overlay specs

With the surface id kept across the navigation, a hidden window's page
now receives the overlay geometry with its first visual properties, so
the rect is already in place when overlay.html's script runs and no
initial geometrychange event is dispatched (a shown window could already
behave this way). Poll navigator.windowControlsOverlay.visible instead,
as the WebContentsView test does; the setBounds() assertion still covers
geometrychange firing on a real change.
